# FinRecon — Stage-3 model provider configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way;
# nothing in this repository reads a key from anywhere but the environment,
# and no key is ever written to a trajectory, a fixture, a log line or an
# exception message.
#
# This file is a template only. Every value below is EMPTY on purpose —
# never commit a real key here.

# --- Credentials ---------------------------------------------------------
# A provider with no key is simply not configured, and the chain skips it
# before the run starts. That is deliberately different from a provider
# whose key is present and rejected: a 401 stops the run rather than
# failing over, because silently switching providers hides a bad key.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Models --------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Each provider has a default in its adapter; these override it.
#
# There is deliberately no shared default across providers: the same model
# ID does not exist on all of them, so a fallback runs a DIFFERENT model, and
# the trajectory records which one actually answered. Provider catalogues
# change faster than this repository does — check the ID against the
# provider's current catalogue before a live run. The run logs it.

# OPENROUTER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# GOROUTER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-thinking
#
# GoRouter routes to upstreams and may resolve an alias to something else.
# The trajectory records the requested ID and the one the API reported
# answering, separately, because a run answered by a substituted model is a
# run whose numbers mean something different.

# --- Endpoints -----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Point at a proxy or a compatible gateway.

# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
# GOROUTER_BASE_URL=https://gorouter.app/v1

# --- Chain behaviour -----------------------------------------------------
# Order is operational availability policy, not a quality ranking.
# Fallback happens ONLY for infrastructure failures (429, 402, 5xx,
# timeout, connection loss). It never happens for a bad tool call, a
# hallucinated candidate ID, an exhausted step budget or an inconclusive
# investigation — those are the model's behaviour, and the safe response is
# to escalate the case, not to ask a different model.

# FINRECON_PROVIDER_ORDER=openrouter,groq,gemini,gorouter
# FINRECON_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# FINRECON_AGENT_TRANSPORT_RETRIES=1
